# Records of phases 1 and 2 brought up to date after phase 3 — part 4. Assessed against the code on 2026-09-27.
#
# How to read this file
#   Each record in UPDATES replaces the record of the same number in the requirement ledger.
#   A record that was PLANNED with no note (Phase 1, never assessed one by one) says in its note what
#   Phase 3 added, and names what earlier phases hold only where that was read in the code or is
#   recorded under another requirement.
#
# Facts that apply to many records below (verified in the code):
#   * NUMI works by patterns over the records (src/numi/engine.ts, src/numi/ops.ts, src/numi/p3.ts). No
#     language model is connected. It reads with the permissions of the person who asks and never acts.
#   * Nothing runs on a schedule. Notices are looked for when a person opens the application
#     (src/ui/Shell.tsx calls refreshNotifications) or presses the button on the Notifications screen.
#   * Nothing leaves the application. A notice is shown inside NUMERO only.
#   * The Digital Twin is arithmetic on monthly rates read from the books. Every result is a SIMULATION.
#   * Imports are CSV files of journals, of opening balances, or of the trial balance of an earlier system.
#   * A status was never lowered. Records that claim more than the code does are left in UNCHANGED and
#     named in the report of this assessment (1191, 1308, 1310).
